{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Standard frame stock for the Frame tool. `section` is what the kernel builds (simplified: no corner radii on steel tube, simplified T-slot); mass in the cut list comes from the built volume and the material density. `fittings` say what goes with the stock: `per` joint (a butt or tee joint, half a mitre or in-line joint), freeEnd (an end that meets nothing) or member. `connectors` declare how other parts plug onto the stock (the start of a connector model: slot type on the faces, end type). `fittings[id].part` is what the kernel builds a fitting from (kind lbracket/gusset/cap/foot, or the dimensions of a T-nut / screw an lbracket names); `spec` is printed in the BOM. A profile's `hardware` lists the fitting ids offered for each place (first = default): `joint` (brackets and gussets at joints), `cap` (free ends), `foot` (free lower ends of legs). `fittings` on a profile are the rest (welds): counted from the joints, not placed.",
